#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""
===============================================================================
 INTENT ANALYSIS  -  single self-contained script
===============================================================================
Input : the flattened turn-level export, saved as CSV, with columns like
        source_row | message_index | classification.intent | message.data.cid |
        message.data.content | message.data.intent_predicted |
        message.data.label | message.data.type | message.type

Output: one HTML report + a folder of CSV tables.

This file has NO local imports. Copy this one file into VS Code, put the CSV
next to it, and run. Nothing else from earlier work is needed.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
 WHAT IS X AND WHAT IS Y
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  X        the text of a USER turn (plus features derived from it)
  y_turn   the intent of that single user turn        <- message.data.label
  y_global the intent of the whole conversation       <- classification.intent

  Assistant turns are NOT X. They are the system's answer and already contain
  the conclusion; using them as input would be target leakage.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
 THE SIX PHASES
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  PHASE 1  DATA ANALYSIS      structure, labels, text, missingness, association
  PHASE 2  CLEANING           mask PII, split roles, strip boilerplate, dedup
  PHASE 3  EDA + PCA          vectorise, compress, is the label learnable at all
  PHASE 4  CLUSTERING         K-means with k chosen by silhouette, heat maps,
                              cluster naming, purity, sub-intent discovery
  PHASE 5  TURN -> GLOBAL     transition matrix, and is the case label just a rule
  PHASE 6  TWO LABEL SETS     Excel label vs a keyword rule block, out of fold,
                              Cohen's kappa, confidence calibration

No column name, class name, keyword or threshold is hardcoded. Everything is
discovered from the file.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
 SETUP
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  pip install pandas numpy scikit-learn scipy matplotlib

  python nora_intent_analysis.py --input intent_labels_all_flattened.csv \\
      --outdir nora_out

  Options
    --salt-file PATH     PII salt (auto-created). Keep it OUTSIDE OneDrive.
    --max-k 30           upper bound for the silhouette search
    --sample 0           0 = use every row
    --min-cluster-size   0 = derived from the data

  If you paste the command from a chat window the double hyphen may be
  auto-converted to an en dash and argparse will reject it. Retype the dashes.
===============================================================================
"""

